.TH LIBMPQ__FILE_STREAM_OPEN 3 2026-09-24 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__file_stream_open \- open a logical MPQ member stream by number.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__file_stream_open(mpq_archive_s *" archive ", uint32_t " file_number ", mpq_file_stream_s **" stream ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open file number \fIfile_number\fP as a decoded logical file stream. The output
is set to NULL before later validation. On success, the stream owns a private
archive clone, begins at logical position zero, and remains usable after the
source archive closes. For custom-I/O archives, the caller must keep the
borrowed callback context valid until this derived file stream closes.
.PP
Open encrypted members whose key cannot be recovered without their plaintext
filename with \fBlibmpq__file_stream_open_name\fP().
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP on success. Otherwise returns an existing archive,
file, clone, allocation, or decoding error and leaves \fI*stream\fP NULL.
.SH ERRORS
\fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST\fP reports an invalid archive, output pointer, file
number, or writer-mode archive.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__file_read (3),
.BR libmpq__file_stream_open_name (3),
.BR libmpq__file_verify (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_close (3)
